# GMS's node is Erda Shower, and the fountain is one of its two halves: the
# player either fires the blast or places the object. Only the object is built,
# because once a character has a matrix it is the half they use; the blast is
# for bosses, and a common node isn't for bosses.
#
# It has its own kill clock: GMS releases the gathered Erda every twelve kills,
# which makes it a mobbing skill only. See Skill.kills_per_cast. GMS's 60-second
# cooldown is on placing the object, not on releases, and the object lasts
# exactly that long, so it is always up and the twelve kills are the whole rule.
#
# Damage is GMS's 450 + 15x: 465% at level 1 and 900% at 30, four lines on ten
# enemies. GMS turns Shadow Partner into final damage for this skill instead of
# a doubled line; here a skill on its own clock gets no Shadow Partner at all,
# the engine's rule for everything the character didn't swing.
name: "Erda Fountain"
description:
  "Plants an object filled with pure Erda. Erda released by defeated enemies "
  "condenses around it, and enough of it gathered is released at once."
kind: SKILL_KIND_AUTO_ATTACK
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_COMMON skill_order: 2 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_COMMON
max_level: 30
max_enemies: 10
lines: 4
kills_per_cast: 12
base { skill_pct: 4.65 }
per_level { skill_pct: 0.15 }
